    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d2">

                <pb facs="0069" n="4" xml:id="pg4"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90H/48</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2570</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-02-26">February 26, 1936</date>.<lb/>[Received March
                        7.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of the Department’s Instruction No. 1198 of February 13, 1936, (File No.
                    711.90H/41), with regard to the proposed agreement with Afghanistan. The
                    Department’s views concerning this matter have been carefully noted, and
                    yesterday morning Mr. Marriner, Counselor of the Embassy, conveyed orally to the
                    Afghan Chargé d’Affaires<anchor n="9" xml:id="d2-f1"/> the viewpoint of the
                    Department and handed to him an English and unofficial French text of the
                    articles of the proposed treaty. A memorandum covering the pertinent portions of
                    their conversation is transmitted herewith.</p>
                <p>In accordance with the Department’s telegraphic Instruction No. 49, February 24,
                    3 P.M.,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d2-f2"/> the Embassy forwarded by air mail on
                    February 25 to the American Ambassador in Moscow copies of the Department’s
                    Instructions, with enclosures, mentioned therein, together with a copy of the
                    memorandum of Mr. Marriner’s conversation with the Afghan Chargé d’Affaires on
                    February 25.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jesse Isidor
                    Straus</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d2-a1.xml" xpointer="d2-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
